\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Now the day is over,
\par Night is drawing nigh,
\par shadows of the evening
\par Steal across the sky.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Now the darkness gathers,
\par Stars their watches keep,
\par Birds and beasts and flowers
\par Soon will be asleep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Jesus, give the weary
\par Calm and sweet repose;
\par With Thy tenderest blessing
\par May their eyelids close.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Grant to little children
\par Visions bright to Thee,
\par Guard the sailors tossing
\par On the angry sea.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Comfort every sufferer
\par Watching late in pain;
\par Those who plan some evil
\par From their sin restrain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Through the long night- watches
\par May Thine angels spread
\par Their white wings above me,
\par Watching round my bed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. When the morning wakens,
\par Then may I arise
\par Pure and fresh and sinless
\par In Thy holy eyes.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Glory to the Father,
\par Glory to the Son,
\par And to Thee, blest Spirit,
\par Whilst all the ages run.
\par                     Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

